+## Infrastructure messages
+
+The *fuzzing-asn1* executable fuzzes the UPER decoders of SPATEM, MAPEM, SREM and SSEM instead of the GeoNetworking router.
+Every input decoded into a valid message is encoded and decoded again; a mismatch aborts, so the fuzzer reports it like a crash.
+Use it with *fuzz.sh* by replacing *fuzzing-persistent* with *fuzzing-asn1*, and investigate findings with *fuzzing-asn1-run*.
+With Clang, `-DFUZZ_WITH_LIBFUZZER=ON` additionally builds *fuzzing-asn1-libfuzzer* for quick runs without AFL++.
+This option instruments the harness only: add `-fsanitize=fuzzer-no-link` and the sanitizers to `CMAKE_C_FLAGS` and `CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS`, otherwise libFuzzer gets no coverage from the decoders in the Vanetza libraries.
+The *input* directory contains one encoded SPATEM, MAPEM, SREM and SSEM each as seeds, generated by the socktap *tlm*, *rlt*, *tlc-request* and *tlc-status* applications.
+`fuzzing-asn1-run <file> spatem` fails unless the file is exactly one valid SPATEM including its ITS PDU header, e.g. to check these seeds.
